summary:
  With nothing on, the desk is told Play can do something only when the list
  has a row.

history:
  Up to 2026.43 the desk's CanPlay was "the list has a row", written apart
  from what Play does. With no station saved, a search result that was
  playing was announced as unplayable, and after its stop the desk's Play
  stayed dark while the widget's own button brought it back. Measured
  2026-11-11 on main.qml's state writer: status Playing, canPlay false.
  2026.44 asks bareplay, the rule a Play that names nothing obeys, so a
  stopped search result and a paused episode count too.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TransportLogic.js

find:
      return bareplay(hasAudition, lastPlay, count, pausedFile).what !== "nothing";

replace:
      return (count | 0) > 0;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_a_playing_audition_can_be_played_with_no_station_saved
  and tests/qml/tst_transportroads.qml::test_with_no_station_saved_a_search_result_can_be_played.
  Line-neutral.
